          "kicker": "Pay transparency",
          "heading": "England's Ellis Genge and Courtney Lawes urge Premiership to publish salaries",
          "body": "England prop Ellis Genge and lock Courtney Lawes have suggested making the wages of all English clubs public, arguing that rugby's secrecy over money is hurting the game commercially. Speaking on The Good, The Bad & The Rugby podcast, Lawes said players are paid peanuts compared with footballers, cricketers and US sport, but that pay cannot outrun what the game earns. Genge said talk of transfer fees is open, unlike talk of pay, and he was surprised his own Leicester contract length was never published."
        },
