          "body": "Former All Blacks scrum-half Justin Marshall has handed Wallabies captain Harry Wilson the top number eight tag, calling him \"the best number eight in the world at the moment\" on The Good, The Bad & Rugby podcast. Wilson's case rests on Eden Park: he made a match-high 27 tackles, scored a try and won a crucial turnover in the 50-19 defeat to the All Blacks. Kieran Read, a former All Blacks number eight, questioned Marshall's \"effortless\" description but agreed Wilson's effort was all there."
